# CabsOnline Part 2

## Public URL
Public deployed application URL: https://web-dev-assignment-2-part-2.vercel.app/

Local development URL used for testing: `http://localhost:3001`

## Standalone Part 2 Scope
CabsOnline Part 2 is a standalone modern web application inspired by the Part 1 taxi booking workflow. It does not reconnect to the Part 1 PHP/MySQL backend, does not use localStorage, and stores booking data in Supabase.

## Technology Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16.2.6 with App Router
- UI library: React 19.2.4 and React DOM 19.2.4
- Language: TypeScript 5
- Database/client: Supabase with `@supabase/supabase-js` 2.106.2
- Map: Leaflet 1.9.4 using OpenStreetMap/CARTO raster tiles
- Address search: Nominatim/OpenStreetMap search API, restricted to New Zealand
- Icons: lucide-react 1.16.0
- Styling: global CSS in `app/globals.css`

## Local Setup
Create `.env.local` with Supabase browser-safe keys:

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key
```

The app also supports `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` as a fallback key name.

Install and run:

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Build for production:

```bash
npm run build
```

## Database
Supabase table: `cabsonline_bookings`

Required columns:

```sql
id BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
booking_ref TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
cname TEXT NOT NULL,
phone TEXT NOT NULL,
unumber TEXT,
snumber TEXT NOT NULL,
stname TEXT NOT NULL,
sbname TEXT,
dsbname TEXT,
pickup_address TEXT,
destination_address TEXT,
pickup_lat DOUBLE PRECISION,
pickup_lon DOUBLE PRECISION,
destination_lat DOUBLE PRECISION,
destination_lon DOUBLE PRECISION,
pickup_date DATE NOT NULL,
pickup_time TIME NOT NULL,
booking_datetime TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
status TEXT DEFAULT 'unassigned',
payment_method TEXT DEFAULT 'Card',
payment_status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending',
driver_id TEXT,
driver_name TEXT,
driver_car TEXT,
driver_plate TEXT,
estimated_fare NUMERIC,
tracking_step INTEGER DEFAULT 1
```

## Microservice And API Endpoints
- Supabase database API: used through `lib/supabaseClient.ts` for booking persistence, payment status updates, driver assignment, tracking updates, and clearing demo data.
- Nominatim address API: `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=json&addressdetails=1&limit=5&countrycodes=nz&q=...`
- OpenStreetMap/CARTO tile service: `https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/light_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png`
- Leaflet marker assets: `https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/images/...`

## Main Features
1. Real map-based interaction: booking and tracking views display pickup and destination markers plus a route line on an interactive Leaflet map.
2. NZ address autocomplete: pickup and destination fields call Nominatim, restrict results to New Zealand, fill address fields, and update map coordinates.
3. Driver/admin management: `/admin` is protected by demo login and supports active booking search, available-driver assignment, driver availability, and clearing demo data.
4. Customer tracking: customers can search by booking reference and see booking received, driver assigned, driver on the way, and trip completed states.
5. Customer-side payment processing: customers pay from the tracking panel; admin cannot process payment.
6. Driver login/workflow: `/driver` lets drivers log in with a demo driver ID, view their trips, and update tracking by confirming on the way, picked up, or finished.

## Routes
- `/`: customer dashboard with Booking, Customer Tracking, Drivers, and Map views.
- `/admin`: admin login and admin dashboard.
- `/driver`: driver login and driver dashboard.

